# shellcheck shell=bash
# Invocation behind output/evaluation/determinism/v100_8978760/, a V100 run
# of the determinism check (hpc/submit_determinism.sh).
#
# Job 8978760 (determinism, account educ-intract), 2026-10-04, 11:22:53 to
# 11:38:34 BST by sacct, ran with these values from the ARC clone
# ~/paper_speech_transcription_audit_w2b at f2578b8, with no modified
# tracked file by its environment record. Slurm gave it one Tesla
# V100-PCIE-32GB (gres/gpu:v100=1; gpu.txt), 8 cores and 48 GB on
# htc-g004, whose processor is an Intel Xeon Platinum 8268. It decoded in
# the checkpoint's float16 with torch's default of 8 threads, under driver
# 580.65.06 and CUDA/13.0.2, and wrote into repro/v100_arm/determinism/
# under $DATA/speech_transcription_env/output/evaluation/. Its log is
# logs/determinism_8978760.out in that clone. A repeat and a second seed
# agreed with its first decode on 200 of 200 utterances. Its summaries,
# gpu.txt and WER report are committed in
# output/evaluation/determinism/v100_8978760/, and
# determinism_cross_accelerator.json compares its hypotheses, which stay in
# that ARC directory, with the other runs under the label v100_seed0.
#
# Why. The comparison had found the L40S run (job 8781724: seed 0, code
# 1bb68ba) and the condition sweep's V100 pass (8917985 task 1: seed 42,
# code 6f9bf56) differing on 2 of the first 200 AMI test utterances, but
# those runs differ in seed, code commit and process as well as in
# hardware, and the sweep's pass decoded the 2 utterances only once. This
# run decoded the same 200 on a V100 with determinism.env's values, seed 0
# twice, as the L40S did, and seed 1 once. Its words match those of the
# sweep's V100 pass, on the same node, on all 200 utterances, so there the
# seed, the code from 6f9bf56 to f2578b8 and the process changed nothing.
# They differ from the L40S's, under the same seed and process, on the
# same 2, and its repeat, which covers both, matches it on all 200. Its
# hypothesis files and WER reports are byte-identical to the CPU arm's
# (job 8978759, same commit and seeds). The comparison still does not part
# the card from its node, or from the code between 1bb68ba and 6f9bf56,
# whose decode-path changes its runs record sets out.
#
# SBATCH_GRES asks Slurm for a V100: sbatch reads it as --gres, and an input
# environment variable overrides the script's own `#SBATCH --gres=gpu:1`
# (man sbatch, Slurm 20.11 on ARC). A --gres on the command line would
# override it in turn, so do not add one.
#
# Reproduce (from the repository root on ARC):
#   ( set -a; . hpc/runs/determinism_v100.env || exit 1; set +a
#     sbatch --account=educ-intract hpc/submit_determinism.sh )
#
# The job writes into $REPORT_DIR/determinism/. Job 8978760 wrote into the
# directory this record named before it ran, given below as the original.
# REPORT_DIR now sends a reproduction to repro/determinism_v100/, so it
# cannot overwrite the ARC copy of that run, which submit_determinism.sh
# would also refuse to do (exit 3) unless OVERWRITE=1.
# original: REPORT_DIR="${DATA}/speech_transcription_env/output/evaluation/repro/v100_arm"
DET_SUITE=ami
DET_LIMIT=200
DET_SEEDS="0 1"
DET_REPEATS=2
SBATCH_GRES=gpu:v100:1
REPORT_DIR="${DATA}/speech_transcription_env/output/evaluation/repro/determinism_v100"
